    {
      "id": "song_07_u4",
      "source_span": "又岂在朝朝暮暮",
      "meaning": "由相聚景象转为判断情意不必以日日相守为条件。"
    }
  ],
  "translations_to_score": [
    {
      "opaque_id": "x73ac0910c5af7d",
      "translation": "Slender clouds weave their finery;
flying stars pass on their sorrow.
Across the vast Silver River, they steal through the dark.
When golden wind and jade dew meet at last,
one moment outshines countless days on earth.

Tenderness flows like water;
their promised meeting, a dream.
How can they bear to look toward the magpie bridge,
the road home?

If two hearts remain true through all the years,
what need have they of day after day, night after night?",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x7b0c9638334e83",
      "translation": "Wisps of cloud weave their delicate designs;
shooting stars bear the ache of parting.
