One meeting in autumn’s golden wind and jade dew
outshines countless lovers’ days on earth.

Tenderness flows like water;
their cherished hour, a dream.
How can they bear to gaze at the magpie bridge,
the road home?

If two hearts endure, steadfast and true,
need they meet morning after morning,
night after night?",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
