      "translation": "Red lotus fragrance fades; autumn chills the jade-smooth mat.\nLightly I loosen my silken robe,\nAnd board the orchid boat alone.\nWho sends a brocade letter through the clouds?\nWhen geese return in written ranks,\nMoonlight fills the western chamber.\nFlowers drift away; water flows on.\nOne longing,\nTwo places of lonely sorrow.\nThere is no way to dispel this feeling:\nOnly just gone from my brows,\nIt rises in my heart.",
