      "translation": "The red lotus fades; the jade mat turns autumn-cold.\nI slip off my silk robe and board the orchid boat alone.\nWho sends a letter through the clouds?\nThe wild geese return in their flight; the moon fills the west tower.\n\nFlowers drift of themselves; water flows on.\nOne longing, two places of quiet sorrow.\nThis ache has no way to be banished:\nIt leaves my brow, then rises in my heart.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
