      "translation": "The red lotus’s fragrance fades; autumn cools the jade mat.\nI loosen my gauze robe and board the orchid boat alone.\nWho sends a silken letter through the clouds?\nWhen the wild geese return in formation, the moon fills the western tower.\nFlowers drift away of themselves; water flows on of itself—\none longing, two places of idle sorrow.\nThis feeling cannot be dispelled:\nno sooner has it left my brow than it rises in my heart.",
      "notes": [
