      "translation": "Red lotus fragrance fades; autumn chills the jade mat.\nSoftly I loosen my silk robe,\nand board the orchid boat alone.\nWho sends a brocade letter through the clouds?\nWhen geese return in lines,\nmoonlight fills the western tower.\n\nFlowers drift away; water flows on.\nOne longing,\ntwo places of quiet sorrow.\nThere is no way to banish this feeling:\njust as it leaves the brow,\nit rises in the heart.",
