{
  "source_poem_zh": "晨起动征铎，\n客行悲故乡。\n鸡声茅店月，\n人迹板桥霜。\n槲叶落山路，\n枳花明驿墙。\n因思杜陵梦，\n凫雁满回塘。",
  "critical_units": [
    {
      "id": "tang_07_u1",
      "source_span": "客行悲故乡",
      "meaning": "行旅途中直接点出对故乡的悲思。"
    },
    {
      "id": "tang_07_u2",
      "source_span": "鸡声茅店月",
      "meaning": "以鸡鸣、客店和月色并置早行时所闻所见。"
    },
    {
      "id": "tang_07_u3",
      "source_span": "人迹板桥霜",
      "meaning": "以桥上人迹和霜痕提示清早已有行人经过。"
    },
    {
      "id": "tang_07_u4",
      "source_span": "因思杜陵梦",
      "meaning": "从当前旅途转入关于杜陵的梦或回想。"
    }
  ],
  "translations_to_score": [
    {
      "opaque_id": "x55af7f2b546599",
      "translation": "At dawn I rise; the travel bells stir.  \nA traveler, grieving for home.  \nRoosters cry; moonlight on the thatched inn;  \nFootprints cross the frost on the plank bridge.  \nOak leaves fall along the mountain path;  \nBitter-orange blossoms brighten the relay-station wall.  \nI think of my dream of Duling:  \nDucks and geese crowd the pond back home.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x2a4d56b2294883",
      "translation": "At dawn I rise and set the journey bells ringing;\nFar from home, I grieve for home.\nCockcrow, a thatched inn, the moon;\nFootprints, a plank bridge, the frost.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain road;\nBitter-orange blossoms brighten the post-house wall.\nAnd I recall my dream of Duling:\nWild ducks and geese fill the curving pond.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xbd425c91c655e1",
      "translation": "Rising at dawn, I set the journey’s bells ringing;\nFar from home, the traveler grieves for home.\nCockcrow, a thatched inn, the moon;\nFootprints, a plank bridge, frost.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain road;\nWhite citrus blossoms brighten the post-house wall.\nAnd I recall my dream of Duling:\nWild ducks and geese fill the curving pond.",
      "notes": [
        "Duling, near the Tang capital of Chang’an, was the poet’s home.",
        "Post-houses were roadside stations offering lodging and fresh horses to official travelers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xd888d5ff938050",
      "translation": "At dawn, the journey bell stirs;\nA traveler mourns his distant home.\nRoosters call beneath the inn’s moon,\nFootprints mark the frosted plank bridge.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain road;\nCitrus blossoms brighten the station wall.\nAnd I think of dreams of Duling—\nDucks and wild geese fill the homeward pond.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xfdd050b24db326",
      "translation": "At dawn I rise; the journey bells begin.\nFar from home, the traveler grieves.\nCockcrow, a thatched inn, the moon;\nFootprints, a plank bridge, the frost.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain road;\nWhite citron blossoms brighten the posting-house wall.\nThen I recall my dream of Duling:\nWild ducks and geese throng the curving pond.",
      "notes": [
        "Duling, near Chang’an, evokes the poet’s home.",
        "The spare third and fourth lines preserve the original’s juxtaposed images."
      ]
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x8b71910cd13b52",
      "translation": "At dawn, the traveler's bells begin to ring;\nA traveler on the road grieves for home.\nCockcrow, thatched inn, moon;\nFootprints on the plank bridge, frost.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain road;\nTrifoliate-orange blossoms brighten the station wall.\nThus I recall my dream of Duling:\nDucks and wild geese fill the returning pond.",
      "notes": []
    }
  ]
}

