  "translations_to_score": [
    {
      "opaque_id": "x4bdcb9975c8529",
      "translation": "At dawn, the travel bells stir;\nI set forth, sorrowing for home.\nCockcrow, a thatched inn, the moon;\nfootprints mark the plank bridge in frost.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain road;\ncitrus blossoms brighten the courier wall.\nThinking then of my Duling dream—\nwild ducks and geese fill the returning pond.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x66a5a5bd78d405",
      "translation": "At dawn I rise; the harness bells ring.\nFar on the road, I ache for home.\nCockcrow, a thatched inn, the moon;\nFootprints, a plank bridge, the frost.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain road;\nBitter-orange blossoms brighten the post-house wall.\nI think again of my dream of Duling:\nWild ducks and geese fill the curving pond.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x59dedcbdd879c3",
      "translation": "At dawn the travelers’ bells stir;\\nOn the road, I grieve for home.\\nCockcrow; a thatched inn beneath the moon.\\nFootprints on the bridge, frost-white.\\nOak leaves fall along the mountain path;\\nBitter orange blossoms brighten the post-station wall.\\nThen I remember a dream of Duling:\\nDucks and geese fill the winding pond.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x8991e6731b393b",
      "translation": "At dawn the travelers stir their bells; \nOn the road, a guest grieves for home.\nCockcrow; moonlight over the thatched inn.\nFootprints on the plank bridge, rimed with frost.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain path;\nBitter orange blossoms brighten the post-station wall.\nAnd so I dream of Duling:\nDucks and geese fill the winding pond.",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "x52646caa56fea9",
      "translation": "Rising at dawn, I set the journey bells ringing;\nFar from home, I grieve for home.\nCockcrow, a thatched inn, the moon;\nFootprints, a plank bridge, frost.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain road;\nWhite orange blossoms brighten the post-house wall.\nThen I recall my dream of Duling:\nWild ducks and geese fill a curving pond.",
      "notes": [
        "Duling is a place associated with the speaker’s longing for home. The final pond scene belongs to the dream.",
        "The orange blossoms are those of the hardy trifoliate orange."
      ]
    },
    {
      "opaque_id": "xf246b35fc35a7f",
      "translation": "At dawn, the traveler sets the journey bells ringing;\nAway from home, he grieves for home.\nA cockcrow, the thatched inn beneath the moon;\nFootprints, frost, and a plank bridge.\nOak leaves fall along the mountain road;\nPoncirus blossoms brighten the post-station wall.\nAnd so he dreams of Duling:\nDucks and geese fill the returning pond.",
      "notes": []
    }
  ]
